hadiths[135]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23451","Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Ubaydillah ibn Adi, he said: Two men informed me that they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj asking him for charity; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his sight over them and lowered it, and saw two sturdy men, and said: If you wish I shall give you from it, but there is no share in it for a rich one nor for a strong earner."
"23452","Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Yasar al-Juhani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that they were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a man of them slept, and some of them went to arrows with him and took them; when the man awoke he was frightened, and the people laughed; he said: What makes you laugh; they said: Nothing except that we took this one's arrows and he was frightened; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to frighten a Muslim."
"23453","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Uthman, meaning Ibn Hakim, Tamim ibn Yazid, freedman of Banu Zama, informed me, from a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us one day, then said: O people, two things, whoever Allah shields from their evil enters Paradise; a man of the Ansar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, do not inform us what they are; then he said: Two things, whoever Allah shields from their evil enters Paradise, until at the third time the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him and said: You see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wants to give us glad tidings but you prevent him; he said: I fear people will rely; then he said: Two things, whoever Allah shields from their evil enters Paradise: what is between his jaws and what is between his legs."
"23454","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdillah, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the killer and the one who commands; he said: Hellfire was divided into seventy parts; for the one who commands sixty-nine, and for the killer one part; and that suffices him."
"23455","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from his father, a neighbor of Khadijah bint Khuwaylid narrated to me, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Khadijah: O Khadijah, by Allah I shall never worship al-Lat, by Allah I shall never worship al-Uzza; she said: Relieve al-Uzza; he said: They were their idol which they worshipped, then they would lie down."
"23456","Asbat narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever repents to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a day before he dies, Allah accepts from him; then he narrated it to another man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hadith, and he said: Did you hear this from him; I said: Yes; he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever repents to Allah half a day before he dies, Allah accepts from him; then another man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated it to me, and said: Did you hear this; I said: Yes; he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever repents to Allah before he dies by forenoon, Allah accepts from him; then he narrated it to another man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you hear this from him; I said: Yes; he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever repents before his soul rattles, Allah accepts from him."
"23457","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People awoke fasting for the completion of thirty; two Bedouins came and testified that they sighted the crescent yesterday; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people and they broke fast."
"23458","Waki narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from the Bedouin, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest."
"23459","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from some of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade continuous fasting and cupping for the fasting one out of sparing his companions, and did not prohibit them."
"23460","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Shabib Abu Rawh, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and recited al-Rum in them, and the recitation became confused for him; when he prayed he said: What is with men who attend prayer with us without purification; those are they who confuse our prayer for us; whoever attends prayer with us, let him perfect purification."
"23461","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Nahdi, from a man of Banu Sulaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counted them on my hand, or on his hand: Glorification is half the Scale, praise be to Allah fills it, takbir fills what is between heaven and earth, fasting is half of patience, and purification is half of faith."
"23462","Waki narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah and Abu al-Dahma, they said: We came upon a man of the desert people and said: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes, I heard him say: You will never leave anything for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, but Allah will replace it for you with what is better for you than it."
"23463","Waki narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran."
"23464","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from an old man of the Ansar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every Muslim is ghusl, perfume, and siwak on Friday."
"23465","Waki narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: We were at this mirbad in Basrah; a Bedouin came with a piece of leather or a piece of sack and said: This is a writing which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me; Abu al-Ala took it and read it to the people, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is a writing from Muhammad, Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh: If you establish prayer, pay zakat, and give from spoils the fifth and the share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the safi, you are secure by Allah's security and His Messenger's security."
"23466","He said: We said: What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: I heard him say: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest."
"23467","Waki narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from his father, from the messenger who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hijrah, and he said: It does not cease as long as the enemy is fought."
"23468","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi, from a man of them, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam on condition of praying two prayers, and he accepted from him."
"23469","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ibn al-Shikhkhir, from the Bedouin, that the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were patched."
"23470","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from his uncle, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine my name and my kunyah."
"23471","Waki narrated to us, Thawr al-Shami narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abu Khirash, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muslims are partners in three: water, pasture, and fire; Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from a man of Aslam, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: If you had said when you entered evening: I seek refuge in Allah's perfect words, all of them, from the evil of what He created, no scorpion would have harmed you until morning."
"23472","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from some of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade cupping for the fasting one and continuous fasting out of sparing his companions; he did not prohibit them; they said: O Messenger of Allah, yet you continue fasting; he said: I am not like one of you; I pass the day fed by my Lord and given drink."
"23473","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih Dhakwan, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree in my wall; command him to sell it to me or give it to me; the man refused; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do it, and for you is a palm tree in Paradise; but he refused; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the most miserly of people."
"23474","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ashath, from his paternal aunt, from her paternal uncle, he said: I was in Dhu al-Majaz market, upon me a striped cloak of mine trailing; a man pricked me with a whip and said: Raise your izar, for it lasts longer and is cleaner; I looked, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I looked, and his izar was to mid-calves."
"23475","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-Ashath, from his paternal aunt Ruhm, from her paternal uncle Ubaydah ibn Khalaf, he said: I came to Madinah as a youth wearing a striped cloak trailing; a man caught me and nudged me with a whip with him, then said: If you raised your garment it would last longer and be cleaner; I turned, and he was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is but a striped cloak; he said: Even if a striped cloak, do you not have in me an example; I looked at his izar, and it was above the ankles and below the calf muscle."
"23476","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from a man of Aslam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, give us rest with prayer."
"23477","Waki narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from Abu al-Aliyah, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I memorized for you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution in the mosque."
"23478","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Mujahid, he said: We were six years under Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah; he stood and addressed us and said: We came to an Ansari man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and entered upon him, and said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and do not narrate to us what you heard from people; we pressed him; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: I warn you of the Masih, and he is wiped of the eye, I think he said: the left; with him travel mountains of bread and rivers of water; his sign: he remains on earth forty mornings; his authority reaches every watering place; he does not come to four mosques: the Kabah, the Messenger's mosque, al-Aqsa mosque, and al-Tur; whatever of that happens, know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed; and Ibn Awn said: I think he said: He is given power over a man, kills him then revives him, and is given no power over other than him."
"23479","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit for dates, and permitted ariyah; ariyah is one palm tree or two which a man buys by their estimate of dates and guarantees them, and he permitted that."
"23480","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from the rider behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or one who narrated to him from the rider behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was riding behind him and his mount stumbled with him, and he said: Wretched is Satan; he said: Do not do that, for he grows great when you say that until he becomes like a mountain and says: By my power I threw him; but when you say: In the name of Allah, he shrinks until he becomes like a fly."
"23481","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah, from a man of the Ansar, he said: I went out with my family intending the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I found him standing, and a man coming toward him; I thought they had a need, so I sat; by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood so long I pitied him for the length of standing; then he left; I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this man kept you standing until I pitied you; he said: Do you know who this is; I said: No; he said: That was Jibril enjoining me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir; indeed had you greeted him he would have returned greeting to you."
"23482","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman informed us, from Anas, that some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he was taken by night, passed by Musa, peace be upon him, standing praying in his grave."
"23483","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari, from a man of Juhaynah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When do I pray the last Isha; he said: When night fills the belly of every valley."
"23484","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Abdillah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah al-Kinani, that he informed him that some of Banu Mudlij informed him that they used to ride rafts in the sea for fishing and carry water with them for travel; prayer overtook them while at sea, and they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If we perform ablution with our water we thirst, and if we perform ablution with sea water we find unease in ourselves; he said to them: Its water is purifying, its dead is lawful."
"23485","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, Yazid said: Sufyan informed us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Aliyah, he said: Thirty of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered and said: What the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites aloud in, we know; what he does not recite aloud in, we do not measure by what he recites aloud in; so they gathered, and no two of them differed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr prayer about thirty verses in the first two rakahs, in each rakah, and in the last two about half of that, and recite in Asr in the first two about half of his recitation in the first two of Zuhr, and in the last two about half of that."
"23486","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I think him Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm is greater in reward than one who does not mix with people nor endure their harm."
"23487","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Jurayy, he said: Two men of Banu Sulaym of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met; one of them said to his companion: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Glory be to Allah is half the Scale, praise be to Allah fills it, Allah is Greatest fills what is between heaven and earth, fasting is half of patience, and ablution is half of faith."
"23488","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, that a man narrated to him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Excellent, excellent for five, how heavy they are in the Scale; a man said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah; he said: There is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, and a righteous child who dies and his parent seeks reward; five, whoever fears Allah with them, certain, enters Paradise: whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and is certain of death, resurrection, and reckoning."
"23489","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Salm narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: A companion of mine narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perish gold and silver; then my companion narrated to me that he went with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, your saying perish gold and silver, what is it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A remembering tongue, a thankful heart, and a wife who helps in the Hereafter."
"23490","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrating from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: One who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment informed me, having opposed its two ends."
"23491","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Zayd Abu al-Hawari, from Abu al-Siddiq, from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Poor believers enter Paradise four hundred years before their rich; I said: Al-Hasan mentions forty years; he said: From the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Four hundred years; until the rich one says: Would that I had been poor; we said: O Messenger of Allah, name them to us by their names; he said: They are those who when there is a disliked matter they are sent for it, and when there is booty others besides them are sent for it, and they are those who are veiled from doors."
"23492","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ghalib al-Qattan narrating from a man of Banu Numayr, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father sends peace to you; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you and upon your father be peace."
"23493","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abdillah ibn Shaqiq, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ibn Abi al-Jada, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall surely enter Paradise of my ummah, by one man's intercession of my ummah, more than Banu Tamim."
"23494","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Zuhayr ibn al-Aqmar, he said: While al-Hasan ibn Ali was addressing after Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, a tall dark man of Azd stood and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing him in his lap saying: Whoever loves me, let him love him; let the witness convey to the absent; were it not for the resolve of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would not have narrated to you."
"23495","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Said ibn Wahb, he said: Ali adjured the people; five or six of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla."
"23496","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Kurdus, he said: He used to narrate stories; he said: A man of Badr's people narrated to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: That I sit in such a gathering is dearer to me than that I free four slaves, meaning storytelling."
"23497","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, he said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Hayyan narrating from Masud ibn Qabisah, or Qabisah ibn Masud, saying: This clan of Muharib prayed Subh; when they prayed, a youth of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The easts and wests of the earth shall be opened for you, and their workers are in Hellfire except one who fears Allah and renders trust."
"23498","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: I said to Jundub: I have pledged allegiance to these, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, and they want me to go out with them to Sham; he said: Hold back; I said: They refuse; he said: Ransom with your wealth; I said: They refuse except that I fight with them with the sword; Jundub said: So-and-so narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slain one comes with his killer on Resurrection Day and says: O Lord, ask this one for what he killed me; Shubah said: I think he said: He says: For what did you kill him; he says: I killed him for so-and-so's dominion; Jundub said: So beware of it."
"23499","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Aqil narrating from Sabiq ibn Najiyah, from Abu Sallam, he said: We were sitting in Hims mosque when a man passed; they said: This one served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so I rose and asked him: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which men did not pass around between you; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim servant says three times in evening or morning: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet, but it is a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to please him on Resurrection Day."
"23500","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Aqil informed me, he said: I heard Sabiq ibn Najiyah, a man of Sham, narrating from Abu Sallam al-Bara, a man of Damascus, he said: We were sitting in Hims mosque, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: He says when he enters morning and when he enters evening: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet, three times in morning and three times in evening, but it is a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to please him on Resurrection Day."
"23501","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Hamid, the associate of al-Ziyadi, narrating from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, narrating from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was taking the pre-dawn meal, and he said: It is a blessing which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you, so do not leave it."
"23502","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Masud, from Humayd ibn al-Qaqa, from a man who kept watching the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would say in his supplication: O Allah, forgive me my sin, and make spacious for me in my circumstances, and bless for me in what You have provided me; then he watched him a second time and he would say the same."
"23503","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Abdullah al-Jufi narrating from Ibn Hasbah or Abu Hasbah, from a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon, and he said: Do you know what al-raqub is? They said: the one who has no child. He said: Al-raqub, the complete raqub, al-raqub, the complete raqub, al-raqub, the complete raqub, is the one who has a child and he died and he did not send forth any of them. He said: Do you know what al-suluk is? They said: the one who has no wealth. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-suluk, the complete suluk, al-suluk, the complete suluk, is the one who has wealth and dies and did not send forth any of it. He said: Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is al-surah? They said: the one who wrestles down. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-surah, the complete surah, al-surah, the complete surah, is the man who becomes angry and his anger intensifies and his face reddens and his hair bristles, then his anger overcomes him."
"23504","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard a man from Banu Layth say: Some people from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, captured me, and I was with them, and they seized sheep and plundered them and cooked them. He said: Then I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Plundered property is not lawful, so overturn the pots."
"23505","Muhammad and Hajjaj both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Minhal or Ibn Maslamah, from his uncle; Hajjaj said: from Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Minhal ibn Maslamah al-Khuzai, from his uncle, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Aslam: Fast today. They said: We have already eaten. He said: Fast the rest of your day, meaning the day of Ashura."
"23506","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Madini, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Uthman ibn Hunayf; al-Qaysi narrated to me that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he urinated, and water was brought, and he poured onto his hand from the vessel and washed it once, and onto his face once, and his forearms once, and he washed his feet once with both his hands, and he said in his narration: his thumb curled."
"23507","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj al-Aslami, and he was their imam, narrating from his father, and he used to perform Hajj with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; Hajjaj said: I think it was Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so when the heat intensifies, delay the prayer."
"23508","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us; Ubayd al-Mukattib informed me, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrating from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which deed is best? Shubah said: Or he said: The best deed is prayer at its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad."
"23509","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Asr, then a man stood praying, and Umar saw him and said to him: Sit, for the People of the Book only perished because there was no separation in their prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ibn al-Khattab did well."
"23510","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from a man, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyena has consumed us. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Other than the hyena is more fearful to me for you than the hyena; the world will be poured upon you abundantly, and would that my nation would not wear gold."
"23511","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from a man from Muzaynah or Juhaynah, he said: The Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when it was a day or two before the sacrifice, would give two jadhahs and take a thaniyyah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The jadhah suffices for what the thaniyyah suffices."
"23512","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Iyad ibn Marthad or Marthad ibn Iyad, from a man among them, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Is any of your parents alive? He said that to him several times. He said: No. He said: Then give water to drink. He said: How do I give it to drink? He said: Suffice them its vessel when they are present, and carry it to them when they are absent from it."
"23513","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Shabib Abu Rawh narrating from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he prayed Fajr and recited al-Rum in it and stumbled in it, and he said: What prevents me? Shubah said: Then he mentioned the patches, and the meaning of his saying: You are not purifying yourselves."
"23514","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us; Asim ibn Kulayb informed me, he said: I heard Iyad ibn Marthad or Marthad ibn Iyad, from a man among them, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a deed that admits him to Paradise, and he mentioned it, except that he said: You suffice them their vessel when they are present, and you carry it to them when they are absent from it."
"23515","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from a man from Banu Amir, that he sought permission upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Shall I enter? Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his servant: Go out to him, for he does not know how to seek permission, and say to him: Let him say: Peace be upon you, may I enter. He said: Then I heard him say that, and I said: Peace be upon you, may I enter. He said: Then he gave permission, or he said: Then I entered, and I said: With what have you come to us? He said: I have not come to you except with good; I have come to you that you worship Allah alone with no partner for Him; Shubah said: And I think he said: alone with no partner for Him; and that you leave al-Lat and al-Uzza, and that you pray by night and day five prayers, and that you fast a month of the year, and that you perform Hajj to the House, and that you take from the wealth of your rich and return it to your poor. He said: Then he said: Has anything of knowledge remained that you do not know? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has known good, and indeed among knowledge is what none knows except Allah: Indeed Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"23516","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever kills a man from among the people of dhimmah will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, or: will not find the scent of Paradise, Mansur is the doubter; its scent is found from a distance of seventy years."
"23517","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Hudhayfah narrating from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I looked at the moon on the morning after Laylat al-Qadr and I saw it as if it were half of a bowl. And Abu Ishaq said: The moon is only like that on the morning after Laylat al-Qadr, and I saw it as if it were half of a bowl. And Abu Ishaq said: It is only on the night of twenty-three."
"23518","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah delivering a sermon in Sham, he said: I heard a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he said about wine: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about wine: If he drinks it, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns the fourth time, kill him."
"23519","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Shall I not guide you to the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: The weak, the wronged. Then he said: Shall I not guide you to the people of the Fire? They said: Yes. He said: Every harsh, arrogant, overbearing person."
"23520","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I met a man who accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as Abu Hurayrah accompanied him, for four years. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us that any of us combs his hair every day, or urinates in his bathing place, or a woman washes with the leftover water of a man, or a man washes with the leftover water of a woman, but they should both scoop together."
"23521","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us; Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Harmalah, informed me, from Ata, that a man informed him that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embracing Hasan and Husayn, saying: O Allah, I love them both, so love them both."
"23522","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us; Malik informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man from Banu Damrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the aqiqah, and he said: I do not like disobedience, as if he disliked the name, and he said: Whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice for his child, let him do so."
"23523","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us; Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, informed us, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah, from Sad ibn Yasar, from a man from Juhaynah, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The disbeliever drinks in seven intestines, and the believer drinks in one intestine."
"23524","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us; Malik informed me, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Salih ibn Khawwat ibn Jubayr, from one who prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Dhat al-Riqa the fear prayer: that a group lined up with him and a group faced the enemy, and he prayed with those with him one rakah, then remained standing, and they completed for themselves, then they left and lined up facing the enemy, and the other group came, and he prayed with them the rakah that remained of his prayer, then remained sitting, and they completed for themselves, then he gave the salutation. Malik said: And this is the most beloved of what I have heard to me regarding the fear prayer."
"23525","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from his father, from Urwah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, he said: A cousin of mine informed me, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a saying and make it brief, perhaps I will grasp it. He said: Do not become angry. He said: Then I repeated to him several times, each time the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned to me: Do not become angry."
"23526","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Juayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khathmi, that he heard Muhammad ibn Kab asking Abd al-Rahman, saying: Inform me of what you heard your father say from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The example of one who plays with dice and then stands and prays is like the example of one who performs ablution with pus and the blood of a pig and then stands and prays."
"23527","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Jurayy al-Nahdi, from a man from Banu Sulaym, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, counted in his hand, or in the hand of al-Sulami, and said: Glory be to Allah is half of the Scale, and praise be to Allah fills the Scale, and Allah is Most Great fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and purification is half of the Scale, and fasting is half of patience."
"23528","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Aws, from a man; the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to him, he said: The caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called on a rainy day: Pray in your dwellings."
"23529","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan informed me; Maryam, the daughter of Iyas ibn al-Bukayr, the Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, from some of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and said: Do you have dharurah? She said: Yes. Then he called for it and placed it on a blister between the toes of his feet, then said: O Allah, Extinguisher of the major and Magnifier of the minor, extinguish it from me, and it was extinguished."
"23530","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid, the associate of al-Ziyadi, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was taking the pre-dawn meal, and he said: Sahur is a blessing which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you, so do not leave it."
"23531","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Israil informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Ali called the people to witness, and said: I adjure by Allah a man who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: O Allah, whomsoever I am his ally, Ali is his ally; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him. He said: Then sixteen men stood and testified."
"23532","Yahya narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Nafi, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from a man from Banu Bakr, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people at Mina on his mount while we were at its forefeet. Ibrahim said: And I do not think him but said: at the Jamarah."
"23533","Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, he said: I heard Zakariyya ibn Sallam narrating from his father, from a man, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saying: O people, hold to the community, and beware of division; O people, hold to the community, and beware of division, three times; Ishaq said it."
"23534","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his grandfather Urwah, from one who narrated to him from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command us to make mosques in our houses, and to improve their construction, and to purify them."
"23535","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sallam ibn Amr al-Yashkuri, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: They are your brothers, so treat them well, and seek their help in what overcomes you, and help them in what overcomes them."
"23536","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, he said: I heard Hassan ibn Bilal narrating from a man from Aslam from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that they used to pray Maghrib with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then return to their families at the farthest part of Madinah, shooting arrows, seeing the landing of their arrows."
"23537","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Zadhan, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from among the Ansar; Shubah said: Or he said: a man from among the Ansar, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in prayer saying: My Lord, forgive me; Shubah said: Or he said: O Allah, forgive me and turn to me, indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving, one hundred times."
"23538","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, he said: I heard a man during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I heard a man in the market of Ukaz saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper, and a man following him saying: This one wants to turn you away from your gods; and it was the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Jahl."
"23539","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi, from a man from Thaqif, one-eyed, called Maruf, and he praised him well, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The wedding feast is a duty, and the second day is customary kindness, and the third day is showing off and ostentation."
"23540","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zara, from Abu al-Ahwas, from some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The recitation of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Zhuhr used to be known by the movement of his beard."
"23541","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I entered with my father upon an in-law of ours from among the Ansar, and prayer came, and he said: O slave girl, bring me ablution water, perhaps I will pray and find rest. Then he saw us disapproving that of him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Rise, O Bilal, and give us rest with prayer."
"23542","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: I heard a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Leave the Abyssinians as long as they leave you, for none will extract the treasure of the Kabah except Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from among the Abyssinians."
"23543","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Dhakwan, from a man from among the Ansar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited a man with a wound, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Call for him the physician of Banu so-and-so. He said: Then they called him and he came, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, does medicine avail anything? He said: Glory be to Allah, has Allah sent down any disease on earth except that He made for it a cure?"
"23544","Rawh narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Dhu Mikhmar, a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Romans will make a secure truce with you, then you and they will raid an enemy, and you will be aided and safe and take booty, then you will return until you alight at a meadow with hills, and a man from among the Christians will raise a cross and say: The cross has overcome. Then a man from among the Muslims will become angry and stand to him and smash it. At that, the Romans will betray and gather for the great battle."
"23545","Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Sulayman, a Madinan, narrated to us; Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb narrated to us, from his father, from his uncle, he said: We were in a gathering, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon us with a trace of water on his head, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we see you content in yourself. He said: Yes. He said: Then the people delved into mention of wealth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no harm in wealth for one who fears Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and health for one who fears Allah is better than wealth, and contentment of self is among blessings."
"23546","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: I saw a man in Madinah with people crowded around him, and he was saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said; and it was a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then I heard him saying: After you is the lying misguider, and his head from behind is knotted, knotted, knotted, three times, and he will say: I am your lord. Then whoever says: You are not our lord, but our Lord is Allah, upon Him we rely and to Him we turn, we seek refuge in Allah from your evil, he will have no authority over him."
"23547","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Jurayy al-Nahdi, that he said: I met an old man from Banu Sulaym at al-Kunasah, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, counted five in his hand, or in my hand, and said: Glorification is half of the Scale, and praise be to Allah fills it, and the magnification fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and fasting is half of patience, and purification is half of faith."
"23548","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, he said: While I was circumambulating the House, a man from Banu Sulaym met me and said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to your people Banu Sad, calling them to Islam? He said: Then I said: By Allah, you said nothing but good, and I hear nothing but good, and I returned and informed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of your saying. He said: O Allah, forgive al-Ahnaf. He said: Then there is nothing I hope for more than it."
"23549","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us; and Abu Jafar al-Khatmi informed me, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Kathir ibn al-Saib, he said: The two sons of Qurayzah narrated to me that they were presented to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the time of Qurayzah, and whoever had grown pubic hair was killed, and whoever had not was left."
"23550","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle of his, that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Say to me a saying that benefits me, and make it brief, perhaps I will retain it. He said: Do not become angry. Then he repeated to him several times, each time the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned to him that he should not become angry."
"23551","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah; my father narrated to me, he said: I went out in the morning for a need, and I came upon a group in the market, and I turned to them, and there was a man narrating to them the description of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and describing his attributes. He said: Then I intercepted him on the open road between Arafat and Mina, and he was raised before me among riders, and I recognized him by the description. He said: Then a man shouted to me: O rider, leave the path of the mounts. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave the rider, for he has a need. He said: Then I came until I took the bridle of the she-camel, or its halter, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, narrate to me, or inform me, of a deed that brings me near to Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: Has that concerned you, or preoccupied you? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then understand, or: comprehend: You worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, and establish prayer, and give zakat, and fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House, and come to people with what you love to be brought to you, and hate for people what you hate to be brought to you. Release the bridle of the she-camel, or its halter. Abu Qatan said: Then I said to him: Did you hear it from him, or did you hear from al-Mughirah? He said: Yes."
"23552","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran informed us, he said: I said to Jundub: I pledged to Ibn al-Zubayr that I would fight the people of Sham. He said: Perhaps you want to say: Jundub gave me a ruling, or: Jundab gave me a ruling. He said: I said: I want that only for myself. He said: Ransom yourself with your wealth. I said: It will not be accepted from me. He said: I was at the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a young boy near puberty, and so-and-so informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The slain will come on the Day of Resurrection clinging to the killer, and he will say: O Lord, ask him why he killed me. Then He will say: For the kingdom of so-and-so. So fear Allah; do not be that man."
"23553","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from his father or his uncle, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the expedition of Tabuk: If plague falls in a land and you are not in it, do not advance upon it, and if it falls in it and you are in it, do not leave it."
"23554","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Amr ibn Aws informed him that a man from Thaqif informed him that he heard the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a rainy day saying: Come to prayer, come to success; pray in your dwellings."
"23555","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, that a man from among the Ansar narrated to him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he laid his sacrifice on its side to slaughter it, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a man: Help me with my sacrifice, and he helped him."
"23556","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us; Yusuf ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Sufyan informed me that Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Amr ibn Hannah informed him, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and from men from among the Ansar from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man from among the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the Conquest, while the Prophet was in a gathering near the Maqam, and he greeted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then said: O Prophet of Allah, I vowed that if Allah grants conquest of Makkah to the Prophet and the believers, I will pray in Bayt al-Maqdis, and I have found a man from among the people of Sham here among Quraysh going with me and returning. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray here. Then the man said this three times, each time the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray here. Then he said his statement the fourth time, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go and pray in it. By Him who sent Muhammad with the truth, had you prayed here, that would have sufficed you for every prayer in Bayt al-Maqdis."
"23557","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Yusuf ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Sufyan informed me that Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Amr ibn Hannah informed him, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from a man from among the Ansar from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man from among the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned it, and he said: Here among Quraysh is an escort of mine, going and returning. Then he said: Pray here, and he mentioned its meaning."
"23558","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Do not become angry. He said: The man said: Then I reflected when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said what he said, and anger gathers all evil."
"23559","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: While I was sleeping, I saw people presented to me wearing shirts, some reaching the breasts, and some reaching below that, and Umar was presented to me wearing a shirt dragging it. They said: How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Religion."
"23560","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the household of Muhammad and his wives and his offspring as You blessed the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious; and bless Muhammad and the household of Muhammad and his wives and his offspring as You blessed the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Ibn Tawus said: And my father used to say the same."
"23561","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Amr al-Qurashi; one who witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, and he ordered the stoning of a man between Makkah and Madinah, and when the stones struck him, he fled, and that reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Why did you not leave him?"
"23562","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Sanani informed us; Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to me, from his father; Fannaj narrated to me, he said: I was working in al-Daynabad, tending therein, and Yala ibn Umayyah came as governor over Yemen, and men from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with him. Then a man from among those who came with him came to me while I was among the crops, diverting water to the crops, with walnuts in his sleeve, and he sat on a water channel, breaking and eating from those walnuts. Then he pointed to Fannaj and said: O Persian, come. Then I drew near him, and the man said to Fannaj: Will you guarantee for me, and I plant from these walnuts by this water? Then Fannaj said to him: What will that benefit me? He said: Then the man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with these two ears of mine, say: Whoever plants a tree and perseveres in guarding it and tending it until it fruits, he will have for everything struck from its fruit a charity with Allah. Then Fannaj said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes. He said: Yes. Then Fannaj said: Then I guarantee it. And from it are the walnuts of al-Daynabad."
"23563","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us; Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his uncle, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came to a place of the house of Yala, Ubaydullah forgot it, faced the House and supplicated. Rawh said: from his father, and Ibn Bakr said: from his mother."
"23564","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muadh, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people at Mina and settled them in their dwellings, and said: Let the Emigrants alight here, and he pointed to the right of the qiblah, and the Helpers here, and he pointed to the left of the qiblah, then let the people alight around them. He said: And he taught them their rites, and the ears of the people of Mina opened until they heard him while in their dwellings. He said: Then I heard him say: Stone the Jamarah with the like of small pebbles."
"23565","Abd al-Samad narrated to us; my father narrated to me, Humayd ibn Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muadh al-Taymi, he said: And he was from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us, and he mentioned the hadith."
"23566","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from a man, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There will be people with a covenant; whoever kills a man among them will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is found from a journey of seventy years."
"23567","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Suhayb came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with dates and bread before him. He said: Come near and eat. Then he took to eating from the dates, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Your eye has inflammation. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I only eat from the other side. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled."
"23568","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Sufyan informed me, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hadrami say: One who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me, he says: Among my nation are people given the like of the rewards of the first of them, denouncing evil."
"23569","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions: Among you are men to whom I do not give anything, entrusting them to their faith, among them Furat ibn Hayyan; he said: from Banu Ijl."
"23570","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, Abu Zumayl Simak narrated to us; a man from Banu Hilal narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one of sound strength."
"23571","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us; Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that a man who served the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for eight or nine years narrated to him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when food was brought near to him, say: In the name of Allah; and when he finished his food, he said: You have fed, and given drink, and enriched, and sufficed, and guided, and chosen; to You is praise for what You have given."
"23572","Muammal ibn Ismail Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Munib, from his uncle, he said: News reached a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever covers his Muslim brother in the world, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection. Then he journeyed to him while he was in Egypt, and asked him about the hadith. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever covers his Muslim brother in the world, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then he said: And I have heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23573","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us; Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, that Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to him that men from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, some of them said: Hijrah has ended, and they differed about that. He said: Then I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, people say hijrah has ended. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hijrah does not end as long as jihad remains."
"23574","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from a man from among the Ansar from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that qasamah existed in the pre-Islamic period, the qasamah of blood, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, affirmed it as it was in the pre-Islamic period, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged by it between people from among the Ansar, from Banu Harithah, in blood they claimed against the Jews."
"23575","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, he said: I heard Ubayd ibn al-Qaqa narrating to a man from Banu Hanzalah, he said: A man watched the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, and he would say in his prayer: O Allah, forgive me my sin, and make spacious for me my circumstances, and bless for me in what You have provided me."
"23576","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Imran, he said: I said to Jundub: I have pledged to these, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, and they want me to go out with them to Sham. He said: Hold back. I said: They refuse. He said: Ransom yourself with your wealth. He said: I said: They refuse unless I strike with them with the sword. Then Jundub said: So-and-so narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The slain will come with his killer on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Lord, ask this one why he killed me. Shubah said: And I think he said: Then He will say: Why did you kill him? He said: Then he will say: I killed him for the kingdom of so-and-so. He said: Then Jundub said: So beware of it."
"23577","Abu Nuh narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pouring water on his head at al-Suqya, either from heat or from thirst, while he was fasting, then he remained fasting until he came to Kadid, then he called for water and broke his fast, and the people broke their fast, and it was the year of the Conquest."
"23578","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted on his journey in the year of the Conquest, and commanded his Companions to break their fast, and said: You will meet your enemy, so strengthen yourselves. Then it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have fasted following your fasting. Then when he came to al-Kadid, he broke his fast. The one who narrated to me said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pouring water on his head from the heat while he was fasting."
"23579","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath, he said: And an old man from Banu Malik ibn Kinanah narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the market of Dhu al-Majaz, walking through it, saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper. He said: And Abu Jahl was throwing dust upon him, saying: O people, let not this one delude you from your religion, for he only wants you to leave your gods and to leave al-Lat and al-Uzza. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not turn to him. He said: We said: Describe the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for us. He said: Between two red garments, of medium stature, full-fleshed, handsome of face, intensely black of hair, intensely white of skin, with flowing hair."
"23580","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from a man from his people, that he used to say during the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab: Uthman ibn Affan will not die until he is made caliph. We said: From where do you know that? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I saw tonight in a dream as if three of my Companions were weighed: Abu Bakr was weighed and outweighed, then Umar was weighed and outweighed, then Uthman was weighed and fell short, while he is righteous."
"23581","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Muhajir Abu al-Hasan, from an old man who met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he passed by a man reciting: Say: O disbelievers. He said: As for this one, he has been absolved from polytheism. He said: And another reciting: Say: He is Allah, One. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise has become due for him."
"23582","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Humran ibn Ayan, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Fulan ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him."
"23583","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from the daughter of Kurduma, from her father, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I vowed to slaughter three of my camels. He said: If it was for a gathering of the gatherings of the pre-Islamic period, or for a festival of the festivals of the pre-Islamic period, or for an idol, then no; and if it was for other than that, then fulfill your vow. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, the mother of this slave girl has a vow of walking; should she walk on her behalf? He said: Yes."
"23584","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi; a freedman of Yazid ibn Nimran narrated to us; Yazid ibn Nimran narrated to us, he said: I met a crippled man at Tabuk and asked him. He said: I passed in front of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a she-ass or a donkey, and he said: He has cut off our prayer; may Allah cut off his trace. Then he became crippled."
"23585","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: The Ansari, the companion of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him, he said: I returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me with what becomes incapacitated of them? He said: Slaughter it, then dye its sandal in its blood, then place it on its side, or on its flank, and do not eat from it, neither you nor anyone of your party."
